<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44457" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sīris</span></b> , is, m.,
		= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σίρις</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The name of a branch of the Nile in Ethiopia</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				5, 9, 10, § 54</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Prisc.
				Perieg. 212</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A river in Italy</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 11,
				15, § 97</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A name for Heraclea in</i> Magna Graecia, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 11,
				15, § 97</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
